- Also note ceiling/floor: D3 with S1 likely ASR≈0 → logit models unstable; pre-register Firth-penalized logistic (or Bayesian weakly informative prior) for quasi-separated cells rather than dropping them.

**Feasibility:** ~1.37M target-model calls total (core 846k + memory grid 192k + moderation 326k + controls 2.4k), ≈ 478M output tokens / 1.2B input tokens, ≈ 53–111 GPU-hours of generation for 7–8B models → ~7–14 h wall-clock on an 8-way serving node. Plus ~240k attacker-LLM calls. Judging is NOT run on every call: 16,000 primary labels (final candidate per cell×behavior) + ~68k trace-audit at 5%. Pre-registered sparsity cut (skip A3×D3) saves ~174k calls (-13%). Requirements outside this environment: GPU serving or inference API, the two attack implementations (AutoDAN, PAIR — NOT in repo), datasets (AdvBench-like + 2 transfer + benign set), judge + guard models, human annotators for the κ audit, and statsmodels/R glmmTMB.

